{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrNzF1RzxdA99VHqQkHr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't see the body of `AuthService.resetPassword`, so this diagnosis is inferred from the call graph and the bug report, not from the code itself.\n\nThe graph shows `resetPassword` (`src/auth/auth.service.ts`, L367) calling only `getForgotSecret`, `findById` and `usersService.update`. It has no edge to a session service. `session.service.ts` appears only through `.create()`, which is used at login and refresh. So a password reset updates the stored password but never deletes the user's existing sessions. A phone that was already signed in keeps a valid session, and `refreshToken` can keep renewing its login.\n\nI'm less sure about the other two candidates. `refreshToken` has no check that the session predates a password change. `usersService.update` doesn't invalidate sessions when the password changes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65498,"cache_read_input_tokens":791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65498},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e942adb7-15b5-499e-867b-f5876efc49ed","uuid":"20198ea6-3a29-4d9c-9817-74d809211a09","timestamp":"2026-11-09T00:07:26.744Z","request_id":"req_011CgrNzEq1itSyqchA19TNg"}
